course: dictionary
lesson: 2371
title: A word from the water: culvert
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A culvert is a tunnel or large pipe that carries a stream or rainwater under a road, railway or path. You may walk or drive over one many times without seeing it.
explain: Its job is to let water pass underneath, so the road or path does not flood. The water goes under, and people and cars go over. Storm culvert is a phrase for one that carries rainwater when a storm comes.
explain: Culverts can be dangerous. «Keep away from storm drains, ditches and culverts, because fast water can sweep a child into a drain pipe.» Never play in or near a culvert.
fact: A culvert is a tunnel or large pipe that carries water under a road, railway or path.
fact: Culvert is a noun: one culvert, many culverts.
fact: A storm culvert carries rainwater, especially when there is a storm.
fact: After rain, the water in a culvert can rise very fast, so never play in or near one.
fact: In «the runnels and their little culverts», runnels are tiny streams and culverts are little tunnels carrying water under a path.
exercise: What is a culvert? | A tall tower built for lookouts | *A tunnel or large pipe that carries water under a road, railway or path | A hedge with sharp thorns
exercise: «They search the hedges, the hollow trees, the runnels and their little culverts.» Find and copy the word that means tiny streams. | trees | hollow | hedges | *runnels
exercise: After heavy rain, what should you do near a culvert? | Race your bike through it | Paddle in it to cool down | *Keep well away, because the water can rise very fast | Play inside it to see the water
test: Why do culverts let water pass under roads? | So that cars can drive through the water | *So that roads and paths do not flood | So that the water can sing | So that fish can swim up the road
test: What is a storm culvert? | *A culvert that carries rainwater, especially in a storm | A drain for old bicycles | A picnic spot by a rainy hill | A place to store storms
exam: Which sentence gives a safety warning about culverts? | Culverts are the best places to hide a ball | Culverts are always shallow, so you can wade through them safely | Culverts are fun to explore on a sunny day | *Keep away from storm drains, ditches and culverts, because fast water can sweep a child into a drain pipe
